    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\ngit\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen reviewing the commit details by `show_at_cursor()`, it would be better we can also include `--stat` option (and consequently `--patch` is also need to included) so that when reviewing the commit, we can have a summary stat to know what files are changed and how many lines are changed.\r\n\r\nThis is my proposed change. But I am not sure if there are any other places which are also need to updated so I created an issue rather than submitting a PR directly.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n lua/mini/git.lua | 2 +-\r\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/git.lua b/lua/mini/git.lua\r\nindex 40a6f78..754213c 100644\r\n--- a/lua/mini/git.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/git.lua\r\n@@ -317,7 +317,7 @@ MiniGit.show_at_cursor = function(opts)\r\n   local is_commit = string.find(cword, '^%x%x%x%x%x%x%x+$') ~= nil and string.lower(cword) == cword\r\n   if is_commit then\r\n     local split = H.normalize_split_opt((opts or {}).split or 'auto', 'opts.split')\r\n-    local args = { 'show', cword }\r\n+    local args = { 'show', '--stat', '--patch', cword }\r\n     local lines = H.git_cli_output(args, cwd)\r\n     if #lines == 0 then return H.notify('Can not show commit ' .. cword, 'WARN') end\r\n     H.show_in_split(split, lines, 'show', table.concat(args, ' '))\r\n\r\n```",
